# Append-only logs: resolve concurrent appends automatically.
#
# `merge=union` is a git built-in — on a three-way merge it keeps BOTH sides'
# lines instead of raising a conflict. DECISIONS.md is a journal: two agents
# appending different entries is not a disagreement, and asking a human to
# resolve it every time is a tax on parallel work with no upside.
#
# Line ORDER after a union merge follows merge order, so only files that are a
# SET of entries belong here. CHANGELOG.md deliberately does NOT: Keep a
# Changelog is newest-first, so its order carries meaning, and union-merging it
# silently interleaved two release lines out of order the first time two
# branches met. A conflict there is the correct outcome — it asks a human where
# the release actually sits.
DECISIONS.md merge=union
